From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Subject: [PATCH] mediatek: give K&R definitions a (void) prototype

GCC rejects a K&R empty parameter list where the kernel's own top-level
Makefile has asked for -Werror=strict-prototypes:

  drivers/misc/mediatek/perf/perf_tracker.c:190:27: error: function
      declaration isn't a prototype [-Werror=strict-prototypes]

Every function touched here already has a (void) prototype in a header -
helio-dvfsrc-opp.h, display_recorder.h, mtk-auddrv-afe.h and
mtk_mfg_counter.h - so the definitions were simply disagreeing with their own
declarations.

Deliberately NOT touched: the twenty chsc_*_node_*_declare() sites in
drivers/input/touchscreen/mediatek/chsc5xxx/. Those look identical to a grep
but are macro invocations -

  #define chsc_version_node_write_declare() \
      chsc_version_node_write(struct file* fp, const char __user *buff, \
                              size_t len, loff_t* ppos)

- so they already expand to a full prototype, and giving them (void) would
break the expansion.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
--- a/drivers/misc/mediatek/perf/perf_tracker.c
+++ b/drivers/misc/mediatek/perf/perf_tracker.c
@@ -187,12 +187,12 @@
 	return 0;
 }
 
-int __attribute__((weak)) get_cur_vcore_uv()
-{
-	return 0;
-}
-
-int __attribute__((weak)) get_cur_ddr_khz()
+int __attribute__((weak)) get_cur_vcore_uv(void)
+{
+	return 0;
+}
+
+int __attribute__((weak)) get_cur_ddr_khz(void)
 {
 	return 0;
 }
